WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:04.400
Perhaps it would be good to start with who we are,

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.840
although Eli gave a little information, but I am part of

3
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:12.030
the trade and investment department of the British Embassy.

4
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.920
Our main goal is to support business relations between

5
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:18.950
Bulgaria and the United Kingdom.

6
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.359
In my day-to-day work this most often means helping

7
00:00:23.359 --> 00:00:26.640
British companies enter the Bulgarian market,

8
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.679
helping them navigate the barriers and

9
00:00:30.679 --> 00:00:34.600
obstacles they see in the market, or simply connecting them

10
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.160
with potential partners.

11
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.710
Quite often, that includes you.

12
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:44.280
On the other hand, we work extremely closely with

13
00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.480
the British-Bulgarian Chamber of Commerce.

14
00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.589
They are our main partner.

15
00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.039
We have a common goal. They unite the businesses of both countries,

16
00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:54.719
both the UK and Bulgaria.

17
00:00:54.719 --> 00:00:58.480
Our shared goal is, as I said, to create opportunities for this

18
00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:05.080
business. On the next slide I have prepared a

19
00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:09.280
so I will try to take a quick look at the overall picture

20
00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:11.830
of exports and imports of both countries.

21
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.560
What can be said at first glance is

22
00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:21.070
that we are looking at statistics from April 2025 to March 2026.

23
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.000
The statistics are based on sources in the UK,

24
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.640
so I apologise if there is any difference from the Bulgarian

25
00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.070
sources. We hope it is not significant.

26
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.709
The trade in goods

27
00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:41.759
and the volume of services traded between

28
00:01:41.759 --> 00:01:46.040
the UK and Bulgaria in this period was about 3 billion

29
00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:50.159
British pounds. That means that compared to the previous period

30
00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:53.550
there is growth of about 3.2%, which is quite positive.

31
00:01:54.079 --> 00:02:00.280
Of this volume, about 1.1 billion is exports from the UK to

32
00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:05.880
Bulgaria. You can see that imports of Bulgarian products and services

33
00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:07.309
into the UK are 1.9.

34
00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:11.280
This means that the UK buys more

35
00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:14.760
than it exports.

36
00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:19.840
The investment statistics for both countries are positive too,

37
00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.120
and for last year we have very encouraging data on

38
00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.080
British investment in Bulgaria.

39
00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:29.789
Growth of over 98%, or almost double.

40
00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:35.519
Part of this is due to large investments in the sector of

41
00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:37.350
green energy and

42
00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:44.879
On the next slide I have shown a slightly more detailed breakdown of

43
00:02:44.879 --> 00:02:48.990
what this actually means, and there are a few things we can say.

44
00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.640
Services make up the largest part of trade for both countries.

45
00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.440
You can see it in red.

46
00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:01.200
About 55% is UK exports of services to Bulgaria, and even

47
00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.110
more for Bulgaria to the UK, nearly 67%.

48
00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:10.879
Growth in services is stable, and growth in exports from

49
00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:15.519
the UK to Bulgaria is stable, with services slightly offsetting

50
00:03:15.519 --> 00:03:16.950
the decline in goods.

51
00:03:17.519 --> 00:03:20.640
The opposite can be said for Bulgaria, where we see more

52
00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.400
significant and steady growth.

53
00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:27.280
As I said on the previous slide, the conclusion is

54
00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:28.180
that the UK

55
00:03:28.959 --> 00:03:30.879
imports more than it exports.

56
00:03:30.879 --> 00:03:34.239
This means there are quite a lot of opportunities for Bulgarian companies and

57
00:03:34.239 --> 00:03:35.429
products in the country.

58
00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.799
Having looked at the overall numbers, let's see what is actually

59
00:03:40.799 --> 00:03:44.439
behind them and what the main goods traded between

60
00:03:44.439 --> 00:03:50.280
the countries are. On the left of the slide you can see the five most

61
00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.239
frequently exported goods from the UK to Bulgaria.

62
00:03:52.239 --> 00:03:55.390
These include medicinal or pharmaceutical products,

63
00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:59.470
specialised equipment, beverages and consumer goods.

64
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.200
You can see that Bulgaria again exports pharmaceutical

65
00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.599
products to the UK. Here grains are in first place,

66
00:04:07.599 --> 00:04:09.270
as well as industrial raw materials.

67
00:04:10.239 --> 00:04:14.079
I already said that the common sector is pharma, and this actually

68
00:04:14.079 --> 00:04:18.000
shows how connected the supply chains are and how actively

69
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.909
companies cooperate in precisely this sector.

70
00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:26.280
On the next slide I show how things stand in the services sector.

71
00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:28.919
Quite similar for both countries.

72
00:04:28.919 --> 00:04:32.830
Transport, tourism, professional services and information technology

73
00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:37.469
are among the main services traded between the two countries.

74
00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:42.520
And I will finish with brief information on the sectors

75
00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:45.880
that we see as priorities for the embassy, or the areas

76
00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:49.840
we work in. One of the areas where we see particularly

77
00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:53.390
great potential is the technology and innovation sector.

78
00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:58.520
The UK is among the leaders in fintech, artificial intelligence and

79
00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:02.800
cybersecurity, and we know Bulgaria has strong positions in software

80
00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:08.080
and engineering services. This creates room for quite a few joint projects

81
00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:13.000
and opportunities. I already said healthcare is one of our common

82
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:19.309
sectors. Pharma and innovation are key for the UK.

83
00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:23.560
On the other hand, Bulgaria has strong expertise and tradition in the

84
00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:27.360
healthcare sector. The sector is being modernised and again offers

85
00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.589
opportunities for cooperation.

86
00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:30.869
Because of the geopolitical

87
00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:35.800
situation, so to speak, and the fact that most governments are investing

88
00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:40.639
ever more resources in the defence sector, we see this sector as

89
00:05:40.639 --> 00:05:43.749
a priority for us, for the UK and for the embassy.

90
00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:49.960
The UK has serious experience in defence technology,

91
00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:51.309
aviation and cybersecurity.

92
00:05:52.199 --> 00:05:57.150
Bulgaria, in turn, has traditions and a generally developed industrial base.

93
00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.910
So, again, a field for cooperation.

94
00:06:02.319 --> 00:06:05.919
The fourth area is the so-called green transition and sustainability.

95
00:06:05.919 --> 00:06:08.840
Sustainable development is among the key topics for business in

96
00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:11.759
the coming years. I think that both for the UK

97
00:06:11.759 --> 00:06:15.630
and for Bulgaria, more and more is invested in green technology,

98
00:06:16.039 --> 00:06:17.149
projects, modernisation.

99
00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:22.039
For us too, or rather for the embassy, the modernisation of

100
00:06:22.039 --> 00:06:24.240
port infrastructure is also important,

101
00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:28.630
which I think is a common topic with the Municipality of Varna.

102
00:06:29.039 --> 00:06:34.520
And last but not least, by volume, consumer goods and brands.

103
00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:37.309
Quality goods are increasingly in demand.

104
00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:42.440
People are ready to pay more for better-quality

105
00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:47.560
products. And in this sector we see great potential in food,

106
00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:52.350
drinks, home goods, beauty, cosmetics

107
00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:58.319
and others. What I can say in conclusion is

108
00:06:58.319 --> 00:07:03.080
that we see growing trade, ever closer ties between

109
00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:06.029
our countries and a lot of untapped potential,

110
00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:11.599
which I hope we will take as an opportunity and together

111
00:07:11.599 --> 00:07:16.280
manage to develop. With that, I give the floor to Eli,

112
00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:19.680
who will tell you a bit more about how things stand in practice and how

113
00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:20.749
we can help you.

114
00:07:22.199 --> 00:07:23.520
Great, thank you very much, Rozi.

115
00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:26.440
I suggest we leave this slide up while I speak,

116
00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:30.879
since many of the things I will mention actually follow

117
00:07:30.879 --> 00:07:34.110
the areas that Rozi has already mentioned.

118
00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:39.319
Just before I forget, let me say how glad I am about

119
00:07:39.319 --> 00:07:42.599
the increase in British cosmetic products in Bulgaria,

120
00:07:42.599 --> 00:07:44.589
because some time ago there were none at all,

121
00:07:45.599 --> 00:07:49.879
and now there is a really great variety, so this was big

122
00:07:49.879 --> 00:07:52.469
news for our whole team when it happened.

123
00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:59.639
I actually want to tell you how, in practice, we support

124
00:07:59.639 --> 00:08:03.759
from the chamber these areas that Rozalina mentioned,

125
00:08:03.759 --> 00:08:08.960
and many others. What we do on a daily or

126
00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:11.029
yearly basis, what happens.

127
00:08:11.599 --> 00:08:15.790
Many of the things we do are in partnership with the embassy,

128
00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:20.800
and with the British Embassy in Bulgaria, as well as the Bulgarian

129
00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.309
Embassy in the UK.

130
00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:28.840
Some of the events that we organise in

131
00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:35.350
the UK are annual, that is, they happen every year.

132
00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:40.839
We have two cocktail receptions at the Bulgarian Embassy,

133
00:08:40.839 --> 00:08:42.680
one in winter and one in summer.

134
00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:49.680
They are purely networking-oriented, but at them we bring together

135
00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.080
the Bulgarian business community in the UK,

136
00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:55.399
our partners in the UK with whom we have worked during

137
00:08:55.399 --> 00:09:00.880
the year. Many of our members, Bulgarian companies, travel to

138
00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:06.040
these events to maintain their network,

139
00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:10.600
to meet people, to get to know the environment,

140
00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:14.079
to look for a niche in which they can grow there.

141
00:09:14.079 --> 00:09:18.519
Here I open a bracket. Our winter cocktail is coming up in early

142
00:09:18.519 --> 00:09:20.629
December, so if any of you

143
00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:26.320
are travelling to the UK, to London, around that time, or would

144
00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:30.680
like to join, as I said, after the event we can

145
00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:35.079
discuss it and tell you how it works,

146
00:09:35.079 --> 00:09:37.990
when it takes place, so that you can plan your trip.

147
00:09:38.519 --> 00:09:39.910
The more targeted

148
00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:44.949
events that we organise are the so-called trade missions.

149
00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:50.000
We organise at least three a year, and the one

150
00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:54.670
that always takes place is for London Tech Week, the biggest tech

151
00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:59.720
event in the UK, which takes place in the second week of June

152
00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:03.440
every year. We always have a business delegation,

153
00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:04.870
for at least ten years now.

154
00:10:05.399 --> 00:10:10.640
The other two delegations, however, we try not to hold in London,

155
00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:14.310
but in other cities where we have reliable partnerships,

156
00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.839
built over the years, whether with local chambers,

157
00:10:17.839 --> 00:10:18.829
or with associations,

158
00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:26.839
that are quite active in developing their businesses in

159
00:10:26.839 --> 00:10:30.360
Europe. Yes, I can give an example.

160
00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:34.910
For example, two weeks ago we had a trade mission to Liverpool

161
00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:39.279
and Hull, on the theme of logistics and transport.

162
00:10:39.279 --> 00:10:43.760
Over the years we have run trade missions to Birmingham,

163
00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:48.880
Manchester, Leeds, Edinburgh, Glasgow, many different cities and on

164
00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:52.030
many different topics such as digital health,

165
00:10:52.959 --> 00:10:56.990
fintech, food and drink, furniture.

166
00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:02.800
I will surely forget some of the areas,

167
00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.829
but it is really very diverse.

168
00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:11.480
And we do all of this based on ideas from companies we talk to.

169
00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:14.800
It is not that we in the team sat down and said we really feel like

170
00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:22.120
doing something. That is, if you have not heard your sector, or

171
00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:25.959
you have, but would like to see something like it again,

172
00:11:25.959 --> 00:11:27.279
we would be glad to discuss it.

173
00:11:27.279 --> 00:11:32.320
We are interested. We talk to business a great deal, and in fact we

174
00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:37.200
draw ideas directly from business on what the next trade missions should be,

175
00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:40.509
where we could go, to look for partnerships,

176
00:11:41.279 --> 00:11:44.720
events you have been to, for example, and found very

177
00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:48.240
useful. We would be glad to think about how we can organise

178
00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.560
a bigger group to go to them.

179
00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:55.279
So that is one more idea of what you can approach

180
00:11:55.279 --> 00:11:58.750
us with after the event, after the official part.

181
00:12:00.279 --> 00:12:06.030
For some time, since last year in fact,

182
00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:11.560
we have also started to organise bootcamps for scale-up companies,

183
00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:15.110
for slightly more grown startups in the UK,

184
00:12:15.519 --> 00:12:21.360
so far we have experience with cybersecurity and fintech,

185
00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:25.430
but of course for next year we are planning

186
00:12:26.399 --> 00:12:30.870
aerospace technologies.

187
00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:36.389
Again, everything is based on ideas from business.

188
00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:40.600
The aerospace one came from just such an idea.

189
00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:44.360
We do not run these bootcamps alone; we run them with partners from all

190
00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:48.990
over Europe. So not only Bulgarian companies take part in them,

191
00:12:49.399 --> 00:12:52.509
but also companies from all over Europe.

192
00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:58.230
So besides getting to know the British potential,

193
00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:03.360
there is also the chance to meet many other organisations from

194
00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:08.440
Europe. Another thing we organise, in fact our biggest

195
00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:13.040
project in the UK so far, in very close

196
00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:17.760
partnership with the British Embassy in Bulgaria and the Bulgarian

197
00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:22.880
Embassy in the UK, is our investment forum,

198
00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:24.470
at which we promote

199
00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:31.800
Bulgaria as an investment destination for British business or

200
00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:34.270
for entrepreneurs from the UK in general.

201
00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:42.240
At it we hold various panels in which we give as examples

202
00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:48.680
good, that is, British investments in Bulgaria and also successful

203
00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:53.000
Bulgarian businesses, to show the strength of the ecosystem in

204
00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:57.790
Bulgaria and how British businesses can grow here.

205
00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:00.749
So far we have had various panel topics.

206
00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:04.990
I am looking at the presentation here to prompt myself and not forget.

207
00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:10.350
We have had fintech, we have had defence,

208
00:14:10.959 --> 00:14:14.870
we have had energy. Last year we also had manufacturing,

209
00:14:15.759 --> 00:14:19.550
and this year we did transport; we had infrastructure.

210
00:14:19.959 --> 00:14:21.710
The topics are very varied.

211
00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:26.639
We plan it for a very long time.

212
00:14:26.639 --> 00:14:29.399
It takes about half a year of talks with businesses,

213
00:14:29.399 --> 00:14:32.030
talks with sponsors, with the embassies,

214
00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:37.350
to agree on the strongest topics of the year.

215
00:14:37.880 --> 00:14:42.519
By strong, understand, for example this year we had very strong

216
00:14:42.519 --> 00:14:45.959
participation by Vodafone, who are investing in Bulgaria now, and we really

217
00:14:45.959 --> 00:14:48.270
wanted to tell that story.

218
00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:50.309
Also taking part were

219
00:14:51.399 --> 00:14:57.829
Baring, Easypay, and many other companies at the forum.

220
00:14:58.399 --> 00:15:02.590
This year it was two weeks ago, on 23 September.

221
00:15:03.079 --> 00:15:06.910
Next year it will be in the autumn.

222
00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:10.279
So once again I will be happy to include topics

223
00:15:10.279 --> 00:15:16.430
that some of you consider important, and with which we can

224
00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:20.680
show Bulgaria in its best light as an investment

225
00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:27.600
destination. And, not exactly last, but still,

226
00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:30.470
we help businesses a great deal

227
00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:35.639
to find trade shows that would be useful for

228
00:15:35.639 --> 00:15:37.440
them. And this works a bit both ways.

229
00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:40.079
On the one hand, businesses tell us which trade shows

230
00:15:40.079 --> 00:15:41.189
were useful to them.

231
00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:44.680
We collect that as information.

232
00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:48.560
We ourselves visit many trade shows in the United Kingdom,

233
00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:51.399
to make sure we have been there in person.

234
00:15:51.399 --> 00:15:54.959
We know what they look like. In pictures and on websites they all look

235
00:15:54.959 --> 00:15:58.710
great, but we try to make sure they are just as good in person.

236
00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:02.150
So that when a new company comes and asks,

237
00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:06.600
shows interest in the market, we can offer them the best

238
00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:11.389
platforms to go through in order to enter the British market.

239
00:16:12.959 --> 00:16:17.230
These are roughly the things we organise in the United Kingdom,

240
00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:21.990
and I would be glad to talk about them with each of you after the event,

241
00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:24.790
if you have ideas, comments or questions.

242
00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:30.389
We have one more big conference that we organise in Bulgaria

243
00:16:31.079 --> 00:16:36.920
in November. This year it will be on 11 November in Sofia, on the theme

244
00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:38.829
Green and Sustainable Cities.

245
00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:43.839
We work very closely on it, we practically organise it

246
00:16:43.839 --> 00:16:50.399
together with the British Embassy in Bulgaria, and the idea is

247
00:16:50.399 --> 00:16:54.600
to share knowledge and good practices between Bulgaria and

248
00:16:54.600 --> 00:17:00.040
the United Kingdom. Local municipalities take part, Varna has

249
00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:03.920
taken part too, as well as local British municipalities.

250
00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:07.959
